{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "131",
   "text": "Why do the U.S., Europe, and China now occupy such different positions in manufacturing trade?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "132",
   "text": "Exports and imports relative to GDP show how economies engage globally",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "133",
   "text": "Not simply how open an economy is",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "134",
   "text": "Import bills must ultimately be covered by income or borrowing",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "135",
   "text": "About one-third of the euro area's level relative to GDP",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#D1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "136",
   "text": "U.S. and euro-area import shares are broadly comparable",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#D2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "137",
   "text": "U.S. deficit ~4–5% of GDP; euro-area surplus ~4%",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#D3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "138",
   "text": "Foreign corporate earnings help finance the U.S. deficit",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#D4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "139",
   "text": "Leaving it exposed to the global manufacturing downturn",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#D5"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "140",
   "text": "Surplus ~7% of GDP; non-processing imports ~4%",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#D6"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "141",
   "text": "'Design here, make abroad' shifts manufacturing production overseas",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "142",
   "text": "Foreign earnings offset part of the manufacturing import bill",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "143",
   "text": "Manufacturing downturns hit Europe especially hard",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#M3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "144",
   "text": "China sells far more manufactures abroad than it buys",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#M4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "145",
   "text": "U.S. imports are not unusually high relative to Europe",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "146",
   "text": "More than domestically produced manufacturing exports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#C2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "147",
   "text": "Its export model is vulnerable when global manufacturing slows",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#C3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "148",
   "text": "Large exports coexist with relatively small manufactured imports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#C4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "149",
   "text": "The U.S. may need to rebuild a stronger manufacturing base rather than finance imports indefinitely",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#K1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "150",
   "text": "Europe and China remain far more manufacturing-oriented, but with very different import structures",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#K2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "151",
   "text": "Some attribute the U.S. goods deficit to comparative advantage in services",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "152",
   "text": "The shale boom reduces the need to export manufactures to pay for oil",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "other_explanation",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#R1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "153",
   "text": "Processing trade makes Europe-China comparisons imperfect",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "154",
   "text": "Europe's export strength also makes it vulnerable to industrial downturns",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_aug_13_19#R2"
  },
